# The /zighud family: help text and answers.
desc.family = Move or hide the shared HUD bar panels.
desc.open = Open the HUD bar settings.
desc.place = Put a panel at a named spot, for yourself.
desc.hide = Hide a panel for yourself, or every panel.
desc.show = Show a panel you hid, or every panel.
desc.default = Set the spot a panel sits at for everyone.
desc.arg.panel = The panel: default (the activity ledger) or grid (the world bars).
desc.arg.placement = The spot, by its id, or "server" to follow the server's choice.
desc.arg.player = Whose HUD to change. Defaults to you.
desc.arg.panel_or_all = The panel, or "all" for every panel. Defaults to all.

open.needsPlayer = Run this in game: the settings are yours, and the console has no HUD.
open.failed = The settings could not be opened.
player.needed = Name a player with --player=<name>, or run this in game.
player.offline = That player is not online.
panel.unknown = No panel is called "{0}". Use default or grid.
placement.unknown = No spot is called "{0}".
placement.unfit = {0} was not measured for {1}, so it is not offered there.
place.done = {0} now sits at {1}.
place.cleared = {0} follows the server's choice again.
place.unchanged = That is already how it is.
hide.done = {0} is hidden.
hide.all = Every panel is hidden.
show.done = {0} shows again.
show.all = Every panel shows again.
default.done = {0} sits at {1} for everyone. Written to {2}.
default.cleared = {0} sits where its shipped file says again. Written to {1}.
default.failed = Could not write to {0}. The file was left as it was.
